==Production==
In August 2024, the [[BBC]] confirmed that ''The Celebrity Traitors'' had been commissioned, along with two more series of ''The Traitors'', [[The Traitors (British TV series) series 3|the first of which]] aired in January 2025.<ref>{{cite web |title=The Traitors: First UK celebrity series announced |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c70j84rvg91o |website=[[BBC News]] |accessdate=13 May 2025 |language=en-gb |date=22 August 2024}}</ref> Speaking at the [[Edinburgh International Television Festival]], Kalpna Patel-Knight, the BBC's head of entertainment, said: "The Traitors has well and truly established itself as an unmissable highlight of the year and the news of a fourth outing, alongside a brand new celebrity version coming to the BBC, will take the series to a whole new level.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Creamer |first1=Jon |title=Traitors confirmed for S4 plus celeb version |url=https://www.televisual.com/news/traitors-confirmed-for-s4-plus-celeb-version/ |website=Televisual |accessdate=13 May 2025 |date=22 August 2024 |archive-date=15 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250515170306/https://www.televisual.com/news/traitors-confirmed-for-s4-plus-celeb-version/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In April 2025, it was confirmed that the show would air in the autumn of that year,<ref>{{cite web |title=BBC's Celebrity Traitors gets exciting update ahead of its 2025 release |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a64349830/celebrity-traitors-release-window/ |website=[[Digital Spy]] |accessdate=14 May 2025 |date=1 April 2025 |archive-date=15 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250515170305/https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a64349830/celebrity-traitors-release-window/ |url-status=live }}</ref> with October 2025 later specified.<ref name=":0" />

Filming for the series began on 22 April 2025 at [[Ardross, Highland|Ardross Castle]] and concluded the following month, consisting of 9 episodes due to air over four weeks from 8 October to 6 November 2025.<ref>{{cite web |title=The Celebrity Traitors launch date confirmed and fans will be treated to an extra-long opening episode |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2025/celebrity-traitors-launch-date-confirmed |website=BBC |format=press release |access-date=21 September 2025 |archive-date=21 September 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250921002202/https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2025/celebrity-traitors-launch-date-confirmed |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Ross |first1=Charley |title=When does Celebrity Traitors start? Here's what we know |url=https://www.glamourmagazine.co.uk/article/when-does-celebrity-traitors-start |website=Glamour UK |accessdate=14 May 2025 |date=25 April 2025 |archive-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250427202318/https://www.glamourmagazine.co.uk/article/when-does-celebrity-traitors-start |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Celebrity Traitors latest: Release date, cast and filming revealed |url=https://www.heart.co.uk/showbiz/celebrity-traitors-start-date-line-up/ |website=[[Heart (radio network)|Heart]] |accessdate=14 May 2025 |language=en |archive-date=15 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250515170305/https://www.heart.co.uk/showbiz/celebrity-traitors-start-date-line-up/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Following the cast announcement, host [[Claudia Winkleman]] said "We're incredibly lucky these brilliant people have said yes. I’d love to say we'll take it easy on them, and they'll just wander round the castle and eat toast for a couple of weeks - but that would be a lie."<ref>{{cite web |title=The BBC's 'Celebrity Traitors' Cast Pits an Olympian Against a 'Ted Lasso' Star |url=https://www.cosmopolitan.com/entertainment/tv/g64759984/celebrity-traitors-cast-line-up-contestants-bbc/ |website=Cosmopolitan |accessdate=14 May 2025 |date=13 May 2025 |archive-date=14 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250514120833/https://www.cosmopolitan.com/entertainment/tv/g64759984/celebrity-traitors-cast-line-up-contestants-bbc/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=The Celebrity Traitors' "brilliant" cast has officially been confirmed – along with a release date window |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a64757349/the-celebrity-traitors-cast-release-window/ |website=[[Digital Spy]] |accessdate=14 May 2025 |date=13 May 2025 |archive-date=13 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250513182707/https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a64757349/the-celebrity-traitors-cast-release-window/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

The first series final was mistakenly released early online in Canada and New Zealand as the episode was mistakenly made available on the [[Crave (streaming service)|Crave]] and [[ThreeNow]] streaming services 24 hours in advance of its broadcast on BBC One, due to a miscommunication between [[All3Media|All3Media International]] and its international partners.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2025/11/celebrity-traitors-uk-leak-canada-all3media-reviewing-processes-1236610470/|title='Celebrity Traitors UK' Distributor All3Media International “Urgently Reviewing Our Processes” After Dramatic Finale Leaks A Day Early In Canada & New Zealand|first=Max|last=Goldbart|date=7 November 2025|accessdate=18 November 2025|archive-date=9 November 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251109123601/https://deadline.com/2025/11/celebrity-traitors-uk-leak-canada-all3media-reviewing-processes-1236610470/|url-status=live}}</ref>

In March 2026, [[BBC]] announced a three-year deal that will keep ''The Celebrity Traitors'' and ''[[The Traitors (British TV series)|The Traitors]]'' in production until 2030.<ref>{{cite web|title=BBC remains Faithful to The Traitors and The Celebrity Traitors until at least 2030|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2026/bbc-remains-faithful-to-the-traitors-the-celebrity-traitors-2030/|publisher=[[BBC]]|accessdate=12 March 2026}}</ref>

